WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.860
Seven airships,

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:06.720
as well as the shipyard 
that serves as a base for them,

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.940
and the two extra-large 
magic stones used to power it.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.750
A dragon golem,

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:13.460
cavalry golems,

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:14.990
soldier golems,

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.660
and the mythril and metals composing them.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:21.380
A new artificial intelligence,

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.140
magic collection panels,

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.130
and Count Ichelberg's research documents...

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:29.000
All of the above shall be 
purchased by the crown,

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.230
while the magic-absorbing 
forced-teleportation magic circle

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:34.110
will be purchased by the magic guild.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.540
Since this was a mandatory quest from 
the king, the reward is increased,

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.320
as is the reward from the adventurers' guild.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.850
As a result, the reward for each person is...

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:46.060
Ahem!

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:49.520
How much is it, Lord Commissioner Ruckner?

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.730
Two million gold coins!

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:55.590
<i>Two million?</i>

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:58.400
<i>So... per person...</i>

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.660
<i>That's a lot!</i>

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:02.450
The reward will be paid in 
installments over 20 years,

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:06.080
and the kingdom shall administer 
all of those payments.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:11.500
What? You're leaving the capital?

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:14.070
I've given it a lot of thought,

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:18.550
and I've decided to base our 
adventures out of Breichburg.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:21.810
I see. It'll be lonely here without you.

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:26.500
But that, too, is part of life!

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:27.760
In that case,

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:31.120
I shall pour all my energy 
into uncovering the culprit

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:35.530
spreading false claims of death so you may 
travel without worry, Baron Baumeister!

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:41.950
False claims of death? Whose death?

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:45.910
Yours, Baron Baumeister!

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.880
People thought I was dead?

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:54.590
Yes. The people were fainting 
when they saw you return alive!

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:58.050
How did such rumors start?

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:01.110
The successful will incur jealousy 
and envy without knowing it,

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:05.540
and find themselves despised 
by people they don't know.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:11.230
Yeah, all of us are still facing some 
harassment just for sticking with Well.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:14.820
On top of that, we're getting 
two million gold now.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:18.310
We'll never be able to 
shake off all that envy.

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:19.950
Speaking of that,

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:27.000
Adventurer's Manual

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:24.370
the adventurers' guild has a system for formally
 disputing the division of a reward, right?

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.520
Shouldn't we just use that?

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:31.500
But that system is typically 
used when a party member's

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.360
division of the reward is too small, isn't it?

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:50.690
Adventurer's Manual

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:39.920
You can use it when you have other 
disputes regarding the division, too.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:43.880
So if we object and say our share 
for this quest is too great...

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:45.280
That's right!

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:50.690
Then we won't have to deal with that 
harassingly large sum of money!

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:54.540
We're already receiving 
plenty from Well as it is.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:59.610
But where would the money 
you free up be redistributed?

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:04.480
What?!

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:07.540
Wait, wait! I don't want that much, either!

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:10.650
By the way, what are you going to do, Elise?

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:15.710
All of my assets belong to Wendelin.

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:21.500
So congratulations on receiving 
ten million gold coins!

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:24.160
<i>They keep piling on reasons to hate me...</i>

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.970
<i>I'm not a bowl of ramen!</i>

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:55.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:55.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:55.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:55.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:55.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:55.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:55.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:55.130
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:02.030
Episode 9
People Hate Me? Are You Kidding Me?!

00:04:57.610 --> 00:05:00.900
Tsk! I can't believe that brat survived.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:03.860
Are you not frustrated, Sir Ruckner?

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:07.820
Wasn't this your chance to come out 
ahead of the Lord Commissioner?

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:10.530
Well, it worked out fine.

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:14.290
After all, many who don't think 
fondly of Baron Baumeister

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:19.780
and those flocking to him have 
now come together right here.

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:23.760
Was that your real goal from the beginning?

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:27.710
True, with this many brought together,

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:30.720
making an annoyance disappear 
would be a simple matter.

00:05:55.610 --> 00:06:01.020
Hey, so I was thinking of having 
someone watch over this mansion

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:03.520
after we move to Breichburg.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:09.330
Yeah, you're currently despised enough 
that someone would proclaim you dead,

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:12.510
so we wouldn't want anyone 
trying anything bad.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:15.660
Then we would need someone who's strong,

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:17.540
capable of maintaining a mansion,

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:19.980
and loyal to Well.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:24.140
You'll never find someone 
who fits the bill that perfectly...

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:29.530
The strong man who won the spearmanship 
division of the martial arts tournament!

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:32.010
He grew up in a merchant family,

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:34.010
so financial affairs are 
a piece of cake for him.

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:37.580
And even though Well's been ignoring 
him these past three years...

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:41.100
He is not deterred from
making his heartfelt appeal.

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:43.450
Roderich!

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:46.380
Oh...

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.710
What?!

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:55.600
Um, I really feel bad asking 
you after all this time...

00:06:56.340 --> 00:07:00.440
But if you're still interested 
in working for me...

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:07.070
I'm so happy!

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:09.280
R-Really?

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:12.700
Are we sure we want this guy?

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:15.350
Well, better him than some weirdo.

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:18.250
Though he's questionable in his own way...

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:21.690
You'll be leaving me in charge 
of your mansion in the capital!

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:22.710
Leaving <i>me</i>!

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:27.670
To think you'd have such faith in me!

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:43.650
Someone's there!

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:45.360
Get down!

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:50.460
I know there was someone there.

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:54.490
It may be the one spreading 
word of Sir Baumeister's...

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:59.410
No, of my lord's death!

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:03.180
Reprehensible fiend!

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:07.840
I, Roderich, promise to discover them!

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:14.260
Even the palace said they couldn't pinpoint 
where the rumors originated, though.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:16.550
Finding them on your own won't be easy.

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:18.760
I'll be fine.

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:23.980
More importantly, my lord, 
the capital is dangerous for you.

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:27.940
It would be wise to leave 
the city as soon as possible.

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:32.490
Actually, there's something 
I still want to do here.

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:53.300
This way, please.

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:59.510
This research lab was constructed with the 
ancient magic civilization as its motif.

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:01.970
Wow.

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:08.940
It's Baron Baumeister, the man who sold 
us the magic circle from the ruins!

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:12.840
I'm the Head Researcher, 
Lucas Götz Beckenbauer.

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:14.400
Nice to meet you.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:20.380
Um, I heard you have a magic circle capable 
of summoning anything the user images?

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:23.180
Yes, this is it.

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:25.820
It's still a prototype,

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:29.630
so depending on the conditions, it may 
require a great deal of magic power,

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:32.530
but in theory, it should be able 
to summon anything to you.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:36.710
Wow, a panty thief would love this.

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:42.000
Please let us make use of it, then.

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:44.270
Sure, go ahead.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.990
The most important thing 
here is your imagination.

00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:53.190
Clearly visualize what you want.

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:55.900
Visualize... Got it.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:57.320
Okay...

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:02.180
Form a clear picture of what I want...

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:03.620
Imagine it...

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:14.000
Wow! It really worked!

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:17.010
Huh? But that's...

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:24.180
Panties?

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:28.100
That's a punch, not panties!

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:31.600
Oh? You summoned the very 
panties she was wearing?

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:34.260
That's the Dragon Slayer for you!

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:38.800
Hold on, hold on, hold on! That's not it!

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:41.060
My imagination just slipped off course

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:44.440
because a panty thief was mentioned!

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:45.740
Hey, listen, she—

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:47.280
I get it.

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:50.420
You can blame me for your perversion,

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:53.210
so let's just hurry up and 
get what we came here for.

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:56.670
I'm not a pervert. I keep it to myself.

00:10:57.670 --> 00:10:58.970
Focus.

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:01.820
Form a clear picture...

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:03.640
Imagine it.

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:05.400
<i>Panties...</i>

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:05.400
<i>To himself...</i>

00:11:07.380 --> 00:11:08.680
Now, come to me!

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:18.820
Here it comes!

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:28.630
Ugh, it stinks!

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:30.370
It smells like entrails.

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:33.360
Oh, Iina, there's blood on your clothes!

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:35.820
Huh?! Oh, no!

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:39.300
It can't be!

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:42.510
We'll need to bathe when we get home.

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:54.190
I knew it.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:56.510
What's he up to?

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:48.940
Wow, even Duke Bleichröder is here.

00:12:49.550 --> 00:12:54.110
Apparently, Well invited him, 
since we'll be in his care in Breichburg.

00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:56.890
So he used his teleportation.

00:12:57.530 --> 00:13:01.070
He wants to thank those 
who have helped him, huh?

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:04.770
A social ploy befitting Baron Baumeister.

00:13:05.460 --> 00:13:08.410
The faces here are giving 
me a sour stomach, though.

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:17.530
Everyone here loves Baron Baumeister,
 for many reasons.

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:21.190
Everyone!

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:25.600
Recently, I used the magic guild's magic circle

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:27.450
to catch these from the northern sea.

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:29.040
It's tuna!

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:36.750
But how are we supposed to eat this?

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:39.060
Huh? We don't eat it as-is?

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:41.770
Um, if you'd like, use this.

00:13:41.770 --> 00:13:46.800
It took three years to develop, 
but I finally completed this soy sauce!

00:14:00.390 --> 00:14:03.390
Tuna with soy sauce is delicious!

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:09.570
Now, please eat up!

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:11.820
We have one more to spare!

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:25.900
The one who spread rumors of your 
death was Head Auditor Ruckner.

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:27.660
Isn't Ruckner...

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:28.970
Yes.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:32.030
He's Lord Commissioner 
Ruckner's younger brother.

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:35.470
But I don't think I've ever met him.

00:14:36.380 --> 00:14:38.850
He was just using you, my lord.

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:43.180
You have strong ties with his brother,

00:14:43.180 --> 00:14:45.980
so he was using you to unseat the 
Lord Commissioner from his position.

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:49.320
They're not on good terms, then.

00:14:49.590 --> 00:14:54.560
He also dispatched a messenger to your home,

00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:58.540
in case you had actually died.

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:00.000
Huh?

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:04.850
Apparently, he was hoping to make your 
eldest brother Kurt indebted to him

00:15:04.850 --> 00:15:08.800
by having his sons inherit after you, 
so that he could gain more influence.

00:15:11.490 --> 00:15:13.760
I can't believe he got my family involved.

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:18.900
The messenger only left a few days ago,

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:22.050
so it will be a while longer 
before he reaches your family.

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:26.940
What a bothersome sibling quarrel.

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:30.900
But he should be quiet for a while now.

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:34.460
I've already taken measures for you.

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:40.040
Sir Ruckner, the town is talking about you!

00:15:40.510 --> 00:15:42.020
Talking about me?

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:47.740
They say that you conspired to see 
Baron Baumeister die in the underground ruins!

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:50.780
Who's spreading such lies?!

00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:56.140
D-Dear, you have a 
messenger from the palace.

00:15:57.090 --> 00:15:58.100
The palace?

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:01.370
Yes, His Majesty has summoned you.

00:16:01.680 --> 00:16:03.060
Tsk!

00:16:04.050 --> 00:16:06.020
You spread a false rumor?

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:07.160
Yes.

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:10.240
I figured the best way to 
fight a rumor was with rumors.

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:14.200
But won't we be in trouble if they find out?

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:18.160
We can just pretend we know nothing about it.

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:20.990
It's ultimately just a rumor, huh?

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:23.120
Which means they can also...

00:16:23.360 --> 00:16:26.730
Yes. He'll face some degree of investigation,

00:16:27.190 --> 00:16:29.310
but he probably won't be punished for it.

00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:32.090
Still, you did a good job 
learning who the culprit was.

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:36.600
I had my suspicions from the start.

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:41.060
That's just the kind of man 
Head Auditor Ruckner is.

00:16:42.510 --> 00:16:43.970
You know him?

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:46.800
He's my father.

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:52.770
Though he's never once 
recognized me as his son.

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:55.900
My mother was a humble merchant's daughter,

00:16:55.900 --> 00:16:59.240
so she could never become a concubine, 
let alone his official wife.

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:01.580
I see.

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:07.410
There's nothing less trustworthy 
than blood ties, in my opinion.

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:10.790
Blood ties, huh?

00:17:11.390 --> 00:17:14.130
Are you all finished discussing your work?

00:17:14.440 --> 00:17:15.720
Oh, yeah.

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:20.030
Roderich, have some if you'd like.

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:21.680
What's this?

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:26.310
It's the fatty tuna that Wendelin 
taught me how to prepare.

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:28.540
It's quite delicious.

00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:31.580
I can't take it anymore.

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:00.050
Hold it!

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:05.180
No way!

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:16.060
It's so good.

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:20.670
Hey, sorry I'm late.

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:22.980
Oh, Wilma.

00:18:24.720 --> 00:18:26.800
Did you already introduce yourself?

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:30.190
What? You know her, Lord Marshall Edgar?

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:32.450
This is Wilma Etol von Asgahan.

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:34.060
My daughter.

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:36.480
I wanted to introduce her to you.

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:39.130
What do you think of Baron Baumeister, Wilma?

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:41.800
I've been investigating you...

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:44.600
To see if you're someone 
who can properly feed me.

00:18:59.440 --> 00:19:00.610
You pass.

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:03.930
Um, I'm glad I passed, but...

00:19:03.930 --> 00:19:07.980
Fatty tuna, fatty tuna, fatty tuna, fatty tuna!

00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:10.020
You want more?

00:19:10.390 --> 00:19:12.380
Please wait a moment.

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:14.840
Fatty tuna, fatty tuna...

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:17.920
Fatty tuna, fatty tuna, 
fatty tuna, fatty tuna...

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:19.580
Sorry about this. Food is more 
important than anything to Wilma.

00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:24.180
I see. Hero syndrome, huh?

00:19:24.710 --> 00:19:26.670
Hero syndrome?

00:19:27.490 --> 00:19:31.140
It refers to those who constantly have 
magic running through all their muscles,

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:35.650
enhancing their body all the time.

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:37.400
Which means...

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:38.570
Fatty tuna!

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:39.780
<i>Fatty...</i>

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:42.740
Fatty tuna!

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:46.430
They have monstrous strength.

00:19:46.430 --> 00:19:50.540
But it also means they're burning 
magic around the clock.

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:54.210
So they have to eat a lot 
to replenish that energy.

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:58.150
Which means feeding them costs, well...

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:03.200
But that shouldn't be a concern 
for you, Baron Baumeister.

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:10.580
She's a glutton, but she looks so young!

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:12.470
What do I do?

00:20:12.470 --> 00:20:15.810
I think I'm feeling maternal instincts!

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:19.330
Wilma, you leave everything to us!

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:23.280
We'll fill you up with fatty tuna!

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:26.240
Fatty tuna!

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:29.200
So there you have it.

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:31.960
How about taking her on as a bodyguard?

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:33.920
Um, I'm...

00:20:34.340 --> 00:20:37.400
You could marry her too, if you'd like!

00:20:37.400 --> 00:20:38.750
Please listen to me!

00:20:39.310 --> 00:20:41.550
Once we return to Breichburg,

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:44.660
we plan to take on hunts 
like normal adventurers.

00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:51.290
So I won't be needing a 
monstrously strong bodyguard.

00:20:52.090 --> 00:20:53.270
Hunts?

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:54.680
What are you talking about?

00:20:54.680 --> 00:20:56.560
You're going to exterminate 
monsters, aren't you?

00:20:57.240 --> 00:20:58.020
Huh?

00:20:58.260 --> 00:20:59.080
Huh?

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:02.900
I'm right, aren't I, Duke Bleichröder?

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:06.700
Where did you hear about that?

00:21:07.190 --> 00:21:10.520
I have plenty of information sources.

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:12.660
Um, what is he talking about?

00:21:12.900 --> 00:21:16.530
The truth is, I have a request for you.

00:21:21.470 --> 00:21:27.050
This says that Wendelin passed away
 while exploring the ancient ruins.

00:21:27.440 --> 00:21:30.010
Wendelin is dead?

00:21:33.440 --> 00:21:38.210
It also says that our children should inherit

00:21:38.210 --> 00:21:41.260
Baron Baumeister's title and 
estate after his passing.
